Thanks you  for using  the LDG  system. We  hope  this
software will give you fully satisfaction.
 
 ÝBWhat's new ?Ýb
 
This release is minor one. 

 - one bug has been fixed on the way LDG looks for a
   library when one specify its path with MiNT convention.
 - the developper C library is now totaly independant on
   the GEM library used. 
Note for developper : 
   as LDG is independant of the GEM library, you need to 
   specify the GEM header file before including 'ldg.h'.
 - LDG and its utilities have been recompiled used the
   last version of Gemlib (pl43).
 
 ÝBRecommandationsÝb
 
Warning, when you start your system with LDG, the LDG
CPX is not necessarly correctly configured. 
  
To simple  users (eg  non LDG-developpers),  read  the
Installation  paragraph   from   the   hypertext   LDG
documentation.
 
This package (C-libraries, tools and the LDG protocol)
is complety free of use, even in a commercial framework. 
Authors refuse all responsabilities in case or malfunction
or problem appeared with the installation or the use
of LDG system. Use it at your own risk.

Additional informations can be found at the internet 
